{"agent":"fleet-failedgate","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":3,"detail":"The helper searches for the *first* run in which the digest appears (`first = next(...)`) and then scans only the runs *after that first occurrence* for a delta that did not re-raise it. It never anchors the search to the run that produced the current FAILED outcome, so a delta that happened *before* the latest failed round is accepted as clearing the finding.\n\nConcretely, given runs for gate `critic` (oldest→newest):\n\n- R1: full round, raises digest `D` → triage records `confirmed`\n- R2: delta round, `delta_raised` lacks `D` (fix looked good at the time)\n- R3: full round, raises `D` again → `it.gate_outcome(\"critic\") == \"failed\"`\n\n`unresolved_review_failure` finds `D` in `found` (taken from `it.gates[\"critic\"].evidence`, i.e. the R3 findings), sees it confirmed, and calls `_cleared_after_delta(runs, D)`. `first` resolves to index 0 (R1), the loop then reaches R2 (`review_kind == \"delta\"`, `status == \"REVIEWED\"`, `delta_raised` present and without `D`) and returns `True`. `left` is therefore empty, the function returns `\"\"`, and `failed_review_blockers` produces no blocker — so `merge`/`complete` ship a gate whose latest outcome is `failed` with a confirmed finding that was re-raised in the failing round and never re-reviewed. That is exactly the escape B85841c0846 is supposed to close. The same hole appears with two deltas (R2 clean, R3 re-raises `D`): the first qualifying delta wins and `True` is returned before the later re-raising delta is ever examined. The check needs to consider only runs at/after the round that yielded the current failed outcome (equivalently, require the *last* relevant delta to not raise the digest).","digest":"a9fd4160dc40d762","location":"ddflow/services/gates/failed_review.py :: `_cleared_after_delta`","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/gates/failed_review.py :: `_cleared_after_delta`"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"4/4 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":18764,"diff_sha":"e650250647520ba9e1400744c7953ca705b2385ba653bd4fe34c238cce5c115d","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":293.8,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","output_digest":"946e5b41ea092843","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B85841c0846.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash.20261017T103248Z-2b7e8fae.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4],"reviewed_head":"858c116ba24a33219c529cac22c737679273c236","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/services/gates/failed_review.py :: `_cleared_after_delta`"],"tree_sha":"858c116ba24a+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"1 finding(s)"},"id":"ef6740f27f02ca8f5bfdb798c","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":74346,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B85841c0846","ts":"2026-10-17T10:37:42.324747Z"}
